Chapter 5: Hardware Description
Arduino Uno
Arduino Uno is the main controller. It reads temperature from the LM35 sensor and controls the fan speed.
Specifications:
Operating Voltage: 5V
Digital Pins: 14
Analog Pins: 6
Flash Memory: 32 KB
LM35 Temperature Sensor
The LM35 measures temperature in degrees Celsius.
Features:
Output: 10 mV per °C
Operating Voltage: 4V–30V
Accuracy: ±0.5°C
L293D Motor Driver
The L293D is used because Arduino cannot directly drive a DC motor.
Functions:
Drives DC motors
Protects Arduino
Supports PWM speed control
DC Fan
The DC fan provides cooling. Its speed changes automatically depending on the temperature.
